<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khasa Malla kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th–14th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Khasa kingdom</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khasa Malla kingdom was a medieval state of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> and adjoining western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sinja">Sinja</a> in the Karnali basin. At its height in the 13th and 14th centuries its kings raided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> and controlled much of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/himalayas">Himalaya</a>. It broke up in the late 14th century into small hill states, among them the Baise principalities and Doti.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khasa-malla-kingdom.jpg" alt="Khasa Malla kingdom" width="320" height="319" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ripu_Malla.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
